{"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "proof", "ucas": "proof cyclic_order", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "proof", "name": "cyclic_order", "axioms": ["int_discrete", "mul_nonneg", "int_domain", "pow_succ", "subgroup_def", "zpksummand_def"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "cyclic_order: forall a:el, S:set, p e k:int: zpksummand(a, S, p, e) and 2 <= p and 0 <= k and k < e -> p^k*a != 0\nroute a: cyclic_order\n    proof\n      fix a S p e k\n      intro hz hp hk hke\n      intro h0\n      obtain M:set st aS sS hM pka hMS hdec hind: a in S and subgroup(S) and subgroup(M) and p^e*a = 0 and (forall x:el: x in M -> x in S) and (forall x:el: x in S -> exists n:int, m:el: m in M and x = n*a + m) and (forall n:int, m:el: m in M and n*a + m = 0 -> exists q:int: n = p^e*q) by zpksummand_def hz\n      have z0: 0 in M by sub_zero hM\n      have c0: p^k*a + 0 = 0 by h0\n      obtain q:int st hq: p^k = p^e*q by hind[p^k, 0] z0 c0\n      have pk: p^e = p^k*p^(e-k) by pow_add[p, k] hk hke\n      have ek: 0 <= e - k - 1 by hke\n      have b: p^(e-k) = p^(e-k-1)*p by pow_succ[p, e-k-1] ek\n      have pq: p^k*(1 - p*(p^(e-k-1)*q)) = 0 by hq pk b\n      have p1: 1 <= p by hp\n      have P1: 1 <= p^k by pow_pos p1 hk\n      cases hc: p^k = 0 or 1 - p*(p^(e-k-1)*q) = 0 by int_domain[p^k, 1 - p*(p^(e-k-1)*q)] pq\n      case h1\n      proof\n        show by h1 P1\n      qed\n      case h2\n      proof\n        have z: 1 = p*(p^(e-k-1)*q) by h2\n        show false by unit_p[p, p^(e-k-1)*q] hp z\n      qed\n    qed\n  rests on:\n    cyclic_order  (96 inferences; axioms: int_discrete int_domain pow_succ zpksummand_def)\n      pow_pos  (32 inferences; axioms: int_discrete mul_nonneg pow_succ)\n      sub_zero  (9 inferences; axioms: subgroup_def)\n      pow_add  (32 inferences; axioms: int_discrete pow_succ)\n      unit_p  (29 inferences; axioms: int_discrete mul_nonneg)\naxioms used:\n  int_discrete   [integer arithmetic] forall n:int: n <= 0 or 1 <= n\n  mul_nonneg     [integer arithmetic] forall a b:int: 0 <= a and 0 <= b -> 0 <= a*b\n  int_domain     [integer arithmetic] forall a b:int: a*b = 0 -> a = 0 or b = 0\n  pow_succ       [integer arithmetic] forall a m:int: 0 <= m -> a^(m+1) = a^m*a\n  subgroup_def   [definition] forall S:set: subgroup(S) <-> (0 in S and (forall x y:el: x in S and y in S -> x + y in S) and (forall x:el: x in S -> -x in S))\n  zpksummand_def [definition] forall a:el, S:set, p k:int: zpksummand(a,S,p,k) <-> (exists M:set: a in S and subgroup(S) and subgroup(M) and p^k*a = 0 and (forall x:el: x in M -> x in S) and (forall x:el: x in S -> exists n:int, m:el: m in M and x = n*a + m) and (forall n:int, m:el: m in M and n*a + m = 0 -> exists q:int: n = p^k*q))\n"}
